From 61f9fa477230118a341f4fd6fb2a9ecba041c2ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:55:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): baseline generated card probes at park time
 [daveey]

A first park on a blocked/review producer woke immediately because the
wait-check default includes those statuses, yet handled_status only knew
about earlier condition_met events. The confirmation observation was not
used, and local confirmation did not even store an observation.

Record local observations and mark generated card probes. Only those
probes use the latest park observation as their implicit baseline; explicit
commands, --until and --from keep their prior behavior. A newer
condition_met keeps precedence. Persist departure inside the generation-
fenced result transaction so blocked -> running -> blocked wakes again.
The 24-hour wake_at backstop is unchanged.

The CLI dry-run hypothesis is confirmed: _cli_wake_check dry-runs the
supplied command before _cli_awaiting generates the default card probe.
No regression assertion requiring an immediate blocked-producer wake was
superseded. An initial metadata-only failure in
 test_continue_still_infers_an_unrelated_live_card exposed unnecessary
marking of inferred card records; the implementation now leaves those
records unchanged and the original assertion passes unedited.

Proof: initial regression file RED on base (10 failures, 3 passes).
GREEN after final rebase: all six requested guards plus 16 new cases,
237 passed. Broader consumer sweep before the final --until preservation
refinement: 79 files, 1917 passed, 1 skipped. scripts/check --base
origin/main: all 20 checks green. Replica cases use the real registry
SQLite reader with unavailable SSH, not mocked verdicts.

Legacy parks have no provenance bit: identical explicit and generated
commands cannot be distinguished retrospectively. They retain existing
behavior until the next park; new generated parks preserve explicit-probe
semantics without guessing from command text alone.

